<script setup>
import { computed, onMounted, onBeforeUnmount, ref } from 'vue';
import { RouterLink } from 'vue-router';
import PortalFooter from '../components/PortalFooter.vue';
const props=defineProps({kind:{type:String,required:true}});
const privacy=computed(()=>props.kind==='privacy');
const contents=computed(()=>privacy.value?['Information handled','Why and who can access it','Security and retention','Your requests']:['Appropriate use','Records and decisions','Availability and changes']);
const mobile=ref(false);let media;
function syncMobile(){mobile.value=media.matches;}
onMounted(()=>{media=window.matchMedia('(max-width:760px)');syncMobile();media.addEventListener('change',syncMobile);});
onBeforeUnmount(()=>media?.removeEventListener('change',syncMobile));
</script>
<template><div class="legal-shell"><header class="legal-header"><RouterLink to="/login" class="legal-brand"><img src="/assets/sbaa-logo.png" alt="" width="48" height="48"/><span>SBAA School Portal</span></RouterLink><nav aria-label="Legal pages"><RouterLink to="/privacy">Privacy Notice</RouterLink><RouterLink to="/terms">Terms of Use</RouterLink></nav></header><main class="legal-content"><div class="legal-title"><p class="eyebrow">SBAA SCHOOL PORTAL · INFORMATION DOCUMENT</p><h1>{{privacy?'Privacy Notice':'Terms of Use'}}</h1><p>{{privacy?'How the current portal handles account and academic information.':'How to use the academic portal responsibly.'}}</p><div class="legal-meta"><span>Version 0.1</span><span>10 October 2026</span><span>Draft · Institutional review pending</span></div></div><aside class="legal-notice" role="note"><strong>Draft for institutional review</strong><p>This Software Engineering 1 project text is not an approved institutional policy. Effective date, official operator/controller, privacy contact, retention schedule, and lawful-basis decisions require Concepcion Holy Cross College review before production use.</p></aside><details class="legal-toc" :open="!mobile"><summary>On this page</summary><nav aria-label="Document sections"><a v-for="(title,index) in contents" :key="title" :href="`#section-${index+1}`">{{index+1}}. {{title}}</a></nav></details><div class="legal-document">
  <template v-if="privacy"><section id="section-1"><h2><span class="legal-section-number">01.</span> Information handled</h2><p>The portal collects the name, student or staff identifier, school email, portal password, optional profile photo and phone, and local appearance preference. It stores password hashes—not your Gmail or institutional mailbox password. School staff can manage enrollment, schedules, grades, announcements, appointment purpose and status, and published firm records. The system records sign-ins, account changes, grades, and other audit events.</p></section><section id="section-2"><h2><span class="legal-section-number">02.</span> Why and who can access it</h2><p>These records support school account access, academic administration, consultations, notices, and security review. Students see only their own enrollment-linked published grades and appointments. Assigned faculty see their classes and consultation requests. Administrators have account and academic management access; appointment oversight excludes purpose text in the current interface. A configured SMTP provider may process message recipient addresses and email content. Legal grounds and the official privacy officer/contact have not yet been approved by the institution.</p></section><section id="section-3"><h2><span class="legal-section-number">03.</span> Security and retention</h2><p>The portal hashes its own passwords, uses revocable sessions and role checks, keeps profile photos and schedule images in private storage, and audits sensitive changes. Development mail writes reset links to a private server log; real delivery needs an approved provider. This project does not claim encryption at rest or independent security certification. Records may be archived, and academic history may remain when an account is closed. Specific retention and deletion periods must be set by the institution.</p></section><section id="section-4"><h2><span class="legal-section-number">04.</span> Your requests</h2><p>Ask the school administrator to review, correct, restrict, or address concerns about your data. The portal does not yet publish an official privacy-contact address. Do not send sensitive details to an unverified contact; obtain the approved contact from the institution.</p></section></template>
  <template v-else><section id="section-1"><h2><span class="legal-section-number">01.</span> Appropriate use</h2><p>Use your own portal account and keep its password private. Do not attempt to access another student’s records, upload harmful content, or misrepresent school information. Faculty and administrators should only use management access for authorized school work.</p></section><section id="section-2"><h2><span class="legal-section-number">02.</span> Records and decisions</h2><p>Portal displays depend on school-maintained data. A new active account does not itself verify identity or link enrollment and grades. Published grades, appointment decisions, and official school actions remain subject to institutional processes; this project does not replace those processes.</p></section><section id="section-3"><h2><span class="legal-section-number">03.</span> Availability and changes</h2><p>This is an academic software project, not an approved production service agreement. Availability, support contacts, governing terms, and institutional approval must be established before deployment with real student data. The portal may maintain security and audit records even when an account is archived.</p></section></template>
  <p>Reading this draft does not constitute consent to optional processing or make the portal legally compliant.</p><RouterLink to="/login">Return to sign in</RouterLink>
</div></main><PortalFooter /></div></template>
